[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Durable Epoch Admission and Feature Qualification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPICE-EPOCH-ADMISSION-001
TITLE: Independent adaptive bounds and inclusive CLI byte limit
STATEMENT: >>>
Adaptive relative tolerance shall lie strictly between zero and one and the
minimum step shall not exceed the supplied finite positive maximum step. Each
bound shall be enforced independently. The CLI shall admit a valid JSON request
of exactly 1,048,576 UTF-8 bytes and reject the next byte with ResourceExhausted.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPICE-EPOCH-REJECTION-001
TITLE: Stable rejection before provider work
STATEMENT: >>>
An AC override with an independently nonfinite real or imaginary component shall
fail with InvalidInput before numerical provider work. An adaptive trial with
a nonfinite coarse or fine component shall fail with InvalidInput. Error message
text is diagnostic context rather than a stable machine error identifier.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPICE-EPOCH-FEATURE-001
TITLE: Feature-specific mutation evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Mutation reports shall retain the enabled feature scope. A mutation in code
compiled out of the tested feature set shall not be classified as numerically
equivalent or caught merely because the default tests pass. Qualification of
the Intel CLI dispatch shall use intel-opencl and actual provider execution.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/epoch_validation_contracts.rs, src/adaptive.rs
independently_nonfinite_trials_are_rejected_by_the_error_boundary, native scoped
mutation replays and docs/epoch-admission-results.md. The frozen 4,411-candidate
campaign is independent of these later development-branch regressions.
<<<
